  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.22 Limited at all times",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.22 \"Limited at all times\" means that the VOC emissions from a source or device, as measured or calculated in accordance with the applicable method(s) and associated averaging times prescribed in Env-A 804, does not exceed the specified emission rate limit for the subject VOC category or subcategory during the RACT-applicable life of the source or device.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1200.html"
